Overlay patch 0055 (D35, narrowed at D40): the LH_PACE probe.
Port of Shipwright-ios 0065 (D-084), by way of Starship-ios 0041.

HISTORY. Through Lighthouse 1.1.x this patch also carried SoH's REAL-TIME TICK
CATCH-UP: GameEngine::ProcessGfxCommands rendered a FIXED number of
interpolated frames per 30 Hz tick, and a pass that overran still delayed the
SP/DP done events the game thread syncs on (measured, D35: 24 tps under 20 ms
of synthetic per-frame load with catch-up off). The catch-up kept a wall-clock
debt and dropped the tick's EARLIEST interpolated frames while it was at least
a frame period.

RETIRED AT 1.2.0 (D40). Upstream d977684f (#597, "Clock-timed frame
interpolation") replaced the fixed sub-frame loop with RunTimedPass
(src/port/Interpolation/FramePacing.cpp): each sub-frame is blended to where
its present lands on the wall clock, the pass stops when another draw would
not finish before the next VI latch, and the RCP task is handed back BEFORE
the last present. That is the catch-up's job done at the source; the seam the
catch-up hooked (the `for (i = 1; i <= subframesPerTick; ...)` loop and
RunCommands' frame-count blend) no longer exists, and layering a second
skip on a pass that already times itself would double-count. So the debt /
skip logic and gSohIos.TickCatchup are gone; gSohIos.PaceStressMs stays, now
as the instrument that shows upstream's pass holding 30 tps under load.

THE PROBE (no behaviour change): one `LH_PACE` line per 10 s beside LH_PERF:
tick wall p50/p95/max + tps, how many ticks got a timed pass, and each 2D
frame split into
  wait  -- inside SetupScreenFramebuffer (nextDrawable / background park)
  busy  -- drawable acquired -> SwapBuffersBegin: the CPU work of the frame
  sleep -- LUS's SyncFramerateWithTime nanosleep pacer
plus thermal and power state (shell SohIos_PowerState: Low Power Mode caps
the panel at 60 Hz). gSohIos.PaceStressMs (default 0, test instrument)
busy-waits that many ms per frame.

Code lives in new files src/port/SohIosPace.{h,cpp} (source of truth:
overlay/assets/probe/); the vendor hunks are call sites only. Generated by
scripts/lh_genlib.py against each file's state just before this patch, so it
regenerates byte-identically from a pristine or a fully patched tree.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/port/SohIosPace.h
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+// LIGHTHOUSE_IOS (overlay 0055, D35/D40): the LH_PACE probe -- shared state for
+// the later probes (0056 spike probe, 0057 menu split). Port of Shipwright-ios
+// 0065 (D-084) via Starship-ios 0041. iOS only. The real-time tick catch-up
+// half was retired at the Lighthouse 1.2.0 bump: upstream's clock-timed pass
+// (d977684f) does that job itself (D40).
+#pragma once
+#ifdef __IOS__
+#include <chrono>
+
+namespace SohIosPace {
+using Clock = std::chrono::steady_clock;
+// Pace seams of the most recent 2D frame (render thread = the main thread):
+//   gDrawBegin  -> gDrawEnd    nextDrawable (SetupScreenFramebuffer)
+//   gDrawEnd    -> gSleepBegin the frame's CPU work
+//   gSleepBegin -> ...         LUS's SyncFramerateWithTime nanosleep pacer
+extern Clock::time_point gDrawBegin, gDrawEnd, gSleepBegin;
+// Interpolation fps of the current tick (frame period = 1000 / gFps ms).
+extern int gFps;
+inline double Ms(Clock::time_point a, Clock::time_point b) {
+    return std::chrono::duration<double, std::milli>(b - a).count();
+}
+inline bool Set(Clock::time_point t) {
+    return t.time_since_epoch().count() != 0;
+}
+} // namespace SohIosPace
+
+extern "C" {
+// Called by GameEngine::SetFrameTiming once per game tick (one RCP task = one
+// tick's display list), just before ProcessGfxCommands, and feeds the LH_PACE
+// report. fps: the pass's target frame rate (interpolation fps for a
+// clock-timed pass, the logic rate otherwise); timed: which pass this tick
+// gets. viPerTick: 60 Hz VIs per tick (2 = BK's 30 Hz, more in cutscenes and
+// demo replays), so the tick period is viPerTick / 60 s exactly.
+void SohIos_PaceTick(int fps, int viPerTick, int timed);
+void SohIos_PaceDrawableBegin(void);
+void SohIos_PaceDrawableEnd(void);
+void SohIos_PaceSleepBegin(void);
+void SohIos_PaceSleepEnd(void);
+int SohIos_ThermalState(void);
+int SohIos_PowerState(void); // shell: 1 LPM, 2 charging, 4 full, 8 unknown
+extern volatile int gSoh3DMode;
+}
+#endif
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/port/SohIosPace.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,123 @@
+// LIGHTHOUSE_IOS (overlay 0055, D35/D40): the LH_PACE probe.
+// Port of Shipwright 0065 (D-084) via Starship 0041. See the patch header.
+// The real-time tick catch-up this file also carried through 1.1.x was retired
+// at the Lighthouse 1.2.0 bump: upstream's clock-timed pass (d977684f) blends
+// each sub-frame by the wall clock and hands the RCP task back before the next
+// VI latch, which is the job the catch-up did (D40).
+#ifdef __IOS__
+#include "SohIosPace.h"
+
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <vector>
+#include <libultraship/libultraship.h>
+#include <spdlog/spdlog.h>
+
+namespace SohIosPace {
+Clock::time_point gDrawBegin{}, gDrawEnd{}, gSleepBegin{};
+int gFps = 60;
+
+static bool sHaveDrawEnd = false;
+static std::vector<double> sWait, sBusy, sSleep, sTick;
+static uint32_t sTimedTicks = 0;
+static Clock::time_point sLastReport = Clock::now();
+
+static double Pct(std::vector<double>& v, double p) {
+    if (v.empty()) {
+        return 0.0;
+    }
+    return v[(size_t)(p * (v.size() - 1))];
+}
+
+static void StressSpin() {
+    // Test instrument (gSohIos.PaceStressMs): a deliberately slow frame, so
+    // tick pacing under load can be proven on a simulator (D35 built it for
+    // the catch-up; since 1.2.0 it exercises upstream's timed pass, D40).
+    int ms = CVarGetInteger("gSohIos.PaceStressMs", 0);
+    if (ms > 0 && ms < 200) {
+        auto until = Clock::now() + std::chrono::milliseconds(ms);
+        while (Clock::now() < until) {
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+static void Report(double tickMs, double tickHz) {
+    sTick.push_back(tickMs);
+    auto now = Clock::now();
+    double el = Ms(sLastReport, now) / 1000.0;
+    if (el < 10.0 || sTick.size() < 8) {
+        return;
+    }
+    for (auto* v : { &sWait, &sBusy, &sSleep, &sTick }) {
+        std::sort(v->begin(), v->end());
+    }
+    size_t n = sTick.size();
+    SPDLOG_INFO("LH_PACE tick_ms p50={:.2f} p95={:.2f} max={:.2f} ticks={} tps={:.2f} tick_hz={:.1f} fps={} frames={} "
+                "wait_ms p50={:.2f} p95={:.2f} max={:.2f} busy_ms p50={:.2f} p95={:.2f} max={:.2f} "
+                "sleep_ms p50={:.2f} p95={:.2f} timed_ticks={} "
+                "stress={} thermal={} power={}",
+                Pct(sTick, 0.5), Pct(sTick, 0.95), sTick.back(), n, n / el, tickHz, gFps, sBusy.size(),
+                Pct(sWait, 0.5), Pct(sWait, 0.95), sWait.empty() ? 0.0 : sWait.back(), Pct(sBusy, 0.5),
+                Pct(sBusy, 0.95), sBusy.empty() ? 0.0 : sBusy.back(), Pct(sSleep, 0.5), Pct(sSleep, 0.95),
+                sTimedTicks, CVarGetInteger("gSohIos.PaceStressMs", 0), SohIos_ThermalState(), SohIos_PowerState());
+    sWait.clear();
+    sBusy.clear();
+    sSleep.clear();
+    sTick.clear();
+    sTimedTicks = 0;
+    sLastReport = now;
+}
+} // namespace SohIosPace
+
+using namespace SohIosPace;
+
+extern "C" void SohIos_PaceDrawableBegin(void) {
+    gDrawBegin = Clock::now();
+}
+
+extern "C" void SohIos_PaceDrawableEnd(void) {
+    gDrawEnd = Clock::now();
+    sHaveDrawEnd = true;
+    sWait.push_back(Ms(gDrawBegin, gDrawEnd));
+}
+
+extern "C" void SohIos_PaceSleepBegin(void) {
+    StressSpin();
+    gSleepBegin = Clock::now();
+    if (sHaveDrawEnd) {
+        sBusy.push_back(Ms(gDrawEnd, gSleepBegin));
+        sHaveDrawEnd = false;
+    }
+}
+
+extern "C" void SohIos_PaceSleepEnd(void) {
+    sSleep.push_back(Ms(gSleepBegin, Clock::now()));
+}
+
+// Lighthouse: a "tick" here is one RCP task (one display list = one game
+// tick), measured on the render thread; the game logic itself runs on its own
+// thread, paced by the 60 Hz VI ticker (src/port/OS/OS_VI.cpp), and syncs on
+// the SP/DP done events the render thread raises -- so a slow render pass can
+// still hold the next tick back, and LH_PACE tps is the arbiter. Since 1.2.0 a
+// clock-timed pass (RunTimedPass) raises them before the next VI latch is due
+// whatever the frame rate; the single-frame pass raises them on return.
+extern "C" void SohIos_PaceTick(int fps, int viPerTick, int timed) {
+    static Clock::time_point sLastTick{};
+    if (fps <= 0 || viPerTick <= 0) {
+        return;
+    }
+    gFps = fps;
+    auto now = Clock::now();
+    double tickHz = 60.0 / viPerTick;
+    double el = 0.0;
+    if (Set(sLastTick)) {
+        el = Ms(sLastTick, now);
+    }
+    sLastTick = now;
+    if (timed) {
+        sTimedTicks++;
+    }
+    if (el > 0.0) {
+        Report(el, tickHz);
+    }
+}
+#endif
